  </figure>

  <p>Same botanical family as coffee. Completely different plant.</p>
  <p>Unlike caffeine, Kratom is dose-dependent. Smaller amounts tend to produce energy and focus. Larger amounts lean toward body ease and relaxation.</p>

  <div class="dose" role="group" aria-label="How the amount changes the experience">
    <div class="dose__cell"><div class="dose__amt">Smaller amounts</div><p class="dose__what">Tend to produce energy and focus.</p></div>
    <div class="dose__cell"><div class="dose__amt">Larger amounts</div><p class="dose__what">Lean toward body ease and relaxation.</p></div>
  </div>

  <p>That dose-dependent range changed the decision for me. I was not choosing between coffee and a different version of coffee. I was choosing a different option for the part of the day when one sharp lift was no longer helping.</p>
  <ul class="stack">
    <li>No neon can.</li>
    <li>No bitter powder ritual.</li>
    <li>No automatic third drink.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>The idea was simple: use a clear starting amount, choose a format that fits a real afternoon, and stop treating the 2 PM slump like a character flaw.</p>

